 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Sticks matter, and this one does too. Find the spot with the least obstructions, usually far from the water and far from lights. That's perfect. Trees are your tent's worst nightmare, wires can damage them badly. Cut it off just above a branch with thick branch tape you can cut off later. Or move somewhere else. Lots of smoke, cold air, and light all night. Tent right next it is the night spot. Move far off to the corner of the field is the day spot. Exactly. Keep a good ten foot from any pipe and twice what you think is safe for a branch length away.",
